// Pull request: #6564 New rules for AI coding agent CLI abuse (Claude Code, Codex CLI)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6564
// Pull request author: yug3009p
// Change: new rule
// Title: Scheduled Task Creation Running AI Coding Agent CLI
// Sigma ID: f168697b-9940-4b19-bfe2-7dfd4a801c69
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Yug Patel
// Date: 2026-11-04 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, T1053.005
// Description: Detects the creation of a scheduled task via "schtasks.exe" whose action runs Claude Code or the
//   OpenAI Codex CLI. A task that runs a coding agent headless gives an attacker a persistent,
//   unattended way to have the agent act on the machine.
// False positives:
//   - Teams that deliberately schedule agent jobs, such as nightly code maintenance
// References:
//   - https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference
//   - https://developers.openai.com/codex/cli/reference
//   - https://github.com/yug3009p/agent-attack-samples
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/5fbbd208eac401b3b5a034335ea3c0dc48014888/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_schtasks_create_ai_agent_cli.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\schtasks.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "schtasks.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "/create" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "claude" or ProcessCommandLine contains "codex")
